## Hazard categories to consider

Use these as a checklist when brainstorming hazards:

| Category | Examples |
|---|---|
| Data integrity | Wrong value, missing value, duplicated value, value on wrong patient |
| Patient identification | Wrong patient matched, patient mis-identified |
| Data availability | Record unavailable when needed, data loss |
| Display correctness | Value displayed incorrectly, unit wrong, context missing |
| Configuration | Wrong config applied, config tampered, missing required config item |
| Cybersecurity | PHI breach, data tampered by attacker, system unavailable |
| Usability | Automation bias, misleading UI, error not noticed |
| Supply chain | SOUP vulnerability, compromised dependency |
| Infrastructure | DB failure, network outage, backup failure |
| Lifecycle | Stale/superseded data shown, version mismatch |

## Probability calibration note

Initial probability estimates are engineering judgements.
They must be updated with real-world field data from PMS (see `../regulatory/pms-plan.md`).
Until then, mark probability estimates as provisional.
